      "q": "11. Find the value of \u2018$k$ \u2019 for which the polynomial ${{x}^{4}}+10{{x}^{3}}+25{{x}^{2}}+15x+k$ is exactly divisible by $(x+7)",
      "a": "Since $p(x)={{x}^{4}}+10{{x}^{3}}+25{{x}^{2}}+15x+k$ is exactly divisible by $(x+7)$ therefore, $(x+7)$ is the factor.\nHence, $p(-7)=0$\n$\\Rightarrow {{(-7)}^{4}}+10{{(-7)}^{3}}+25{{(-7)}^{2}}+15(-7)+k=0$\n$\\Rightarrow 2401-3430+1225-105+k=0$\n$\\Rightarrow k=91$."
