      "q": "25. The given figure depicts a racing track whose left and right ends are semi-circular. The difference between the two inner parallel line segments is $$60$$\nm and they are each $$106$$ m long. If the track is $$10$$\nm wide, find:\n(i). The distance around the track along its inner edge.",
      "a": "(i)\nThe distance around the track along the inner edge:\n$$\\Rightarrow 106+106+(\\pi \\times 30+\\pi \\times 30)$$\n$$\\Rightarrow 212+\\dfrac{22}{7}\\times 60$$\n$$\\Rightarrow \\dfrac{2804}{7}m$$\n(ii). The area of the track.\nAns. (ii)\nThe area of the track:\n$$\\Rightarrow 106\\times 80-106\\times 60+2\\dfrac{1}{2}\\pi [{{40}^{2}}-{{30}^{2}}]$$\n$$\\Rightarrow 106\\times 20+\\pi (70)(10)$$\n$$\\Rightarrow 12+700\\times \\dfrac{22}{7}$$\n$$\\Rightarrow 4320{{m}^{2}}$$"
