      "a": "It is known that, there are $366$ days in a leap year containing $52$weeks and $2$ days.\nThese two days can be $$\\left( MT \\right),\\left( TW \\right),\\left( W\\text{ }Th \\right),\\left( Th\\text{ }F \\right),\\left( FS \\right),\\left( SS \\right),\\left( SM \\right)$$. Now, since, $52$ weeks contain $52$ Mondays, so the remaining Monday can be obtained if the two days are $$\\left( MT \\right)$$ or $$\\left( SM \\right)$$, that is, $2$ out of $7$ cases. Thus, the probability of having $53$ Mondays in a leap year $=\\frac{2}{7}$."
